@module_doc("""
A Petal program drawn as its dataflow diagram, written entirely in Petal.

Three modules, re-exported here:

- `ptl_dataflow/extract`: `dataflow_graph(ir, natives, source)` folds the
  compiler's user-only IR into one node per binding;
- `ptl_dataflow/layout`: `layout_graph(g)` lays that out left to right (or top to bottom), with
  functions and loops as boxes, and `collapse(g, ids)` folds boxes;
- `ptl_dataflow/view`: `dataflow_viewer(r, source, compiled)` is the
  interactive viewer (code and diagram, linked).

```petal ignore
import ptl_dataflow
let g = dataflow_graph(out.ir, out.natives, source)
let l = layout_graph(g)
```

The IR comes from the host: `dataflow_ir(source)` in petal-web-canvas, or
`petal show-ir --json --user-only`.
""", see: ["ptl_dataflow/extract", "ptl_dataflow/layout", "ptl_dataflow/view"])

pub import ptl_dataflow/extract
pub import ptl_dataflow/layout
pub import ptl_dataflow/view
